# T-SELECT-RECT — REAL-input drag-rectangle atom for variant3d (TEST-S1).
#
# Owns ONLY this file. No game code, config, manifest, fixture, gate or git edit.
# AUTHORING ONLY: no Godot process was started by the author; this atom has NOT
# been run. It is deliberately allowed to FAIL pre-fix on the overlay checks.
#
# What it proves (unlike uitest.gd:115-123, which calls _set_selection directly):
#   * InputEventMouseButton(press) -> InputEventMouseMotion(left mask) ->
#     InputEventMouseButton(release) travels through C3Input._unhandled_input()
#     (input_controller.gd:528,556-663) and produces a real box selection.
#   * The 6 screen-pixel port threshold (input_controller.gd:613,662-663) and
#     the donor's 0.005 m world-ground epsilon (DSEL-01 claim 1;
#     onmousemove.inc:32-34) are both crossed by the synthetic drag; both are
#     MEASURED and asserted, not assumed.
#   * Donor Shift=add (DSEL-01 claim 4) is recorded as an expectation in the
#     result JSON; the port's drag branch ignores Shift (input_controller.gd:624,
#     DSEL-01 claim 27) so it is a declared divergence, not silently dropped.
#   * cmd_* side effects are counted through a C3Game subclass spy installed on
#     input_ctl.game only; the sim itself stays the real booted game.
#   * A CanvasLayer selection-rect overlay with Rect2 == Rect2(p0,p1).abs()
#     during drag, hidden after release, is ASSERTED. Pre-fix this fails
#     (EXPECTED_FAILURE) because world3d.gd:126-127 stores sel_rect/sel_active
#     with no draw consumer (V3D-01 break point 1; DSEL-01 claim 28). The
#     assertion is retained, never weakened or deleted.
#
# Capture path: real 64x64 game boot via res://scenes/main.tscn with --config
# <small_map_64.json> and a --screenshot path used ONLY as the menu-skip flag
# (main.gd:206,230-244,1096-1097). Headless: main's screenshot saver is disabled
# after boot; no PNG is the assertion surface. A self-owned SubViewport was
# rejected: it would duplicate main's proven boot/capture seam and still would
# not draw the missing marquee (V3D-01 section 4).
#
# Launch form (NOT run by the author; one Godot at a time, Windows `python`):
#   python variant3d\tools\godot_runner.py run --id <ticket>-S1 --timeout 40 -- \
#     --headless --path variant3d --script res://tests/t_select_rect.gd -- \
#     --config <ABS>\variant3d\tests\fixtures\small_map_64.json \
#     --screenshot <temp>\smallmap64_select_rect.png
# Exit via call_deferred("quit", 0/1); result at res://tests/results/t_select_rect.json.
extends SceneTree

